  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9f3b10ad4d1f4b6aa84f8f6d5e9a19c0, type: 3}
  m_Name: text_greed_deep
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AncientTextData
  textId: greed_deep
  title: The Same Six
  body: 'We counted them, once, thinking the count would protect us. Greed. Lust.
    Wrath. Sloth. Pride. Envy. Six sicknesses, six islands, and at the end of each,
    a crown to break. We told ourselves the number was arbitrary, that other heroes
    in other years must have faced other trials. We were wrong. It is always these
    six. It has always been these six.


    Understand what that means before you
    decide how to feel about it. You are not the first to bleed on Greed''s golden
    sand. Others stood here with your same certainty, your same borrowed trust, your
    same weapons in unfamiliar hands. They won. They wrote this. And then they were
    gone.


    We do not say this to frighten you. We say it because the truth,
    met early and met plainly, hurts less than the truth that ambushes you later.
    Read on when you are ready. Some of you will want to. Some of you will slam the
    book shut. Both are allowed.'
